<title>USA: IPO FILING - Fulcrum Direct Inc.</title>
<headline>IPO FILING - Fulcrum Direct Inc.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Company Name		 Fulcrum Direct Inc</p>
<p>Stock symbol			FLCM</p>
<p>Estimated price range	   $10-$12/shr</p>
<p>Total shares to be offered    2.5 million</p>
<p>Shrs offered by company	  2.5 million</p>
<p>Shrs outstanding after ipo    8,916,953</p>
<p>Lead Underwriter		Hambrecht &amp; Quist</p>
<p>Underwriters over-allotment  375,000 shrs  </p>
<p>Business: Fulcrum, based in Rio Rancho, N.M., is a direct marketer of proprietary children's apparel brands, including After the Stork, Playclothes, SunSkins and Discount Direct. Use of Proceeds: To repay $3 million principal amount of subordinated debt plus accured interest, to purchase trademarkets in connection with certain of the company's brands for about $1.75 million, to purchase the company's headquarters, call center and distribution center for about $2.5 million in cash, to fund potential acquisitions and for working capital and general corporate purposes.</p>
<p>Financial Data in 000s in year ended:</p>
<p>				Dec 28, 1996	 Dec 30, 1995</p>
<p>   - Revenue		 $36,457		 $28,581</p>
<p>   - Net Income		 $614		    $320</p>
